  "description": "Read-Through Cache is a caching strategy where the application always reads data through the cache layer. On a cache miss the cache itself (or the service layer) is responsible for loading the data from the underlying data store, storing it, and returning it to the caller.\n\t\tThis pattern offloads the origin database from repetitive reads and serves subsequent requests at memory speed.\n\t\tUpdate: Now Framework use used to Cache Hash Items.",
